<title>JAPAN: Japan Telecom share trade suspended - TSE.</title>
<headline>Japan Telecom share trade suspended - TSE.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in Japan Telecom Co Ltd shares has been suspended for Wednesday's session, the Tokyo Stock Exchange said.  </p>
<p>The TSE said the shares were suspended due to unclear information about a possible merger involving the company.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on Wednesday that the telecommunications firm was planning to merge with International Telecom Japan Inc (ITJ) later this year to compete with the giant carrier Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT).</p>
<p>Terms of were not yet set, but it was likely to be a stock-for-stock merger of about five ITJ share for one Japan Telecom share, the newspaper said.</p>
</text>
